1 (3) Additional conditions, requirements, and restrictions as the Secretary
2 may deem necessary to implement the requirements of this chapter. This may
3 shall include requirements concerning reporting, recording, and inspections of
4 the operation of the site.
5 * * *
6 § 1531. MANUFACTURER AND DISTRIBUTOR PARTICIPATION IN
7 PRODUCER RESPONSIBILITY ORGANIZATION
8 (a) No manufacturer or distributor may sell or distribute a beverage
9 container in this State without participating in a Secretary-approved producer
10 responsibility organization.
11 (b) On or before January 1, 2027, manufacturers or distributors of beverage
12 containers sold or distributed within the State shall apply to the Secretary to
13 form a producer responsibility organization to fulfill the requirements of
14 manufacturers or distributors under this chapter.
15 (c) The Secretary may approve, for a period not longer than 10 years, the
16 producer responsibility organization, provided that:
17 (1) the producer responsibility organization or its subsidiary is
18 registered under 26 U.S.C. § 501(c)(3) as a nonprofit entity;
19 (2) the producer responsibility organization has the capacity to
20 administer the requirements of a stewardship plan required by section 1532 of
21 this title; and

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE AND SENATE H.915
2026 Page 11 of 69
1 (3) the producer responsibility organization does not create any
2 unreasonable barriers to joining the producer responsibility organization and
3 shall take into the consideration the needs of small manufacturers that do not
4 generate a significant volume of containers.
5 (d) After approval, the producer responsibility organization shall maintain
6 a website that identifies:
7 (1) the name and principal business address of each manufacturer or
8 distributor participating in the producer responsibility organization;
9 (2) the name of each beverage and the container size covered by the
10 stewardship plan; and
11 (3) for each beverage container subject to the plan, a Universal Product
12 Code and a barcode shall be displayed on the container.
13 (e) If the producer responsibility organization fails to implement the
14 requirements of this chapter, the rules adopted by the Secretary, or an approved
15 stewardship plan, the Secretary may dissolve the producer responsibility
16 organization.
17 (f) If no producer responsibility organization is formed, the Secretary shall
18 either require the formation of the producer responsibility organization or
19 adopt and administer a plan that meets the requirements of section 1532 of this
20 title. If the Secretary administers the plan adopted under section 1532, the
21 Secretary shall charge each manufacturer or distributor the costs of plan

